 deletion, a clear, popitem), on a getset added, and on an"] [121 1 "// MRO set (c3MRO's and readyTypes'), so an answer is never older than the namespaces it was read from."] [129 1 "// lookupAttrMRO is _PyType_Lookup's walk: t's MRO's dicts, then the getsets and slot wrappers of each."] [150 1 "// superLookup is lookupAttr over the part of start's MRO after typ (super's lookup)."] [179 1 "// descrGet is a found attribute's __get__ (obj nil: from the class); a built-in method found on a"] [180 1 "// built-in type is bound to obj (its value for a built-in subclass's instance)."] [186 3 "// object's methods take the instance itself (PY6d's REQUEST: __reduce_ex__'s class); objectDescr is"] [187 3 "// methodDescrs[b] == ObjectType without the map's lookup on every method's binding (queue 210)"] [199 1 "// methodDescrs are the built-in types' methods that left their type's dict through the class (T.name: CPython's"] [200 1 "// method_descriptor), each with its type: put in a class's dict (socket.socket.getsockname = saved, test_socket's"] [201 1 "// test_injected_authentication_failure) such a method still binds to the instance, as a method descriptor does,"] [202 1 "// where a built-in function there (class A: f = len) does not."] [207 1 "// instanceDict is o's __dict__, nil when it has none."] [238 1 "// The attribute instructions' inline caches (202b; PEP 659's LOAD_ATTR and STORE_ATTR caches, after the type"] [239 1 "// version tag): load-attr and store-attr of an object whose type takes the generic path keep, per instruction, the"] [240 1 "// type they last saw and lookupAttr's answer for it, valid while typeEpoch has not moved (the epoch the type"] [241 1 "// attribute cache's own answers hold by, attr.go's lookupAttr), so a hit compares two words where lookupAttr hashes"] [242 1 "// the name into the type's cache."] [248 2 "// di: where the instance's dict held the name when it was last found there (queue 210; CPython's"] [249 2 "// LOAD_ATTR_INSTANCE_VALUE's index): an entry holding the name's very str (co_names are interned) is the name's"] [253 1 "// lookupAttrAt is lookupAttr(tp, name) through the cache of c's instruction pc."] [259 1 "// attrSite is an instruction's caches: the last types it saw, the latest first (queue 210: richards' four task"] [260 1 "// classes share their methods' instructions, and one entry missed at every change of type)."] [265 1 "// attrICAt is c's instruction pc's cache entry holding lookupAttr(tp, name)."] [287 34 "// tp's old entry, else the oldest, dropped"] [292 1 "// dictEntryAt is the position of the entry of d holding name itself, through the hint *di (kept up to date); -1"] [293 1 "// when d does not hold name (an equal str in its place is found, but not kept as the hint)."] [305 1 "// loadAttrAt is load-attr at c's instruction pc: GetAttr, its generic path's lookup through the instruction's cache."] [314 3 "// genericGetAttrFound's instance dict through the hint (queue 210)"] [336 1 "// storeAttrAt is store-attr (v nil: delete-attr) at c's instruction pc: SetAttr, its generic path's lookup through"] [337 1 "// the instruction's cache."] [346 3 "// genericSetAttrFound's dict.Set through the hint: a value replaced in place (queue 210)"] [355 21 "// the usual case: the name inserted last"] [362 1 "// GenericGetAttr is object.__getattribute__."] [369 1 "// genericGetAttrFound is GenericGetAttr with lookupAttr's answer for o's type tp."] [387 1 "// GenericSetAttr is object.__setattr__ (v nil: object.__delattr__)."] [394 1 "// genericSetAttrFound is GenericSetAttr with lookupAttr's answer for o's type tp."] [422 1 "// typeGetAttr is type.__getattribute__: the metatype's data descriptors, then the type's MRO, then"] [423 1 "// the metatype's other attributes."] [436 29 "// a method descriptor leaving its type"] [444 4 "// a built-in type's class and static methods know their type for __qualname__"] [467 1 "// typeSetAttr is type.__setattr__: a class's attribute, its slots updated for a special one."] [478 3 "// tp_name: a static type's module and name ('compression.zstd.ZstdCompressor'; builtins' bare)"] [498 1 "// SetAttr is setattr(o, name, v); v nil is delattr."] [506 1 "// DelAttr is delattr(o, name)."] [509 1 "// GetAttrOptional is getattr(o, name) with nil, not an AttributeError, when there is no such attribute."] [512 1 "// LookupSpecial is a special method's lookup on o's type (_PyObject_LookupSpecial): bound to o, or nil."] [521 1 "// getAttrOptional is getattr(o, name, None) without the None: nil when there is no such attribute."] [533 1 "// callBound calls a method found on self's type bound to self (CPython's vectorcall of an unbound"] [534 1 "// method with self first, or __get__ then the call); owner is the type of self's MRO it was found on"] [535 1 "// (lookupAttr's), nil when not known."] [542 4 "// wrapperdescr_call's check (bpo-37619: a wrapper of the wrong class in a class's dict)"] [548 4 "// a built-in function in a class's dict is no method descriptor: called without the instance, as"] [549 4 "// descrGet's rule and lookup_maybe_method (class C: __call__ = len; typing.NewType's __call__ = _idfunc,"] [550 4 "// queue 207)"] [554 4 "// object's own methods take the instance itself (descrGet's rule, PY6d's R2), as for"] [555 4 "// object.__reduce_ex__ of a class deriving from a built-in type (PY6g's F2: random.Random's pickling)"] [611 2 "// a descriptor's own attributes (PY6a: inspect's getattr_static reads __name__ and __objclass__)"] [624 2 "// object's attributes"] [626 2 "// a built-in type with a dictionary shows it itself (BaseException's, function's, module's); a class's is"] [627 2 "// subtype_getsets_full's, in the dict of the class that adds it (addLayoutDescrs): object has none"] [635 2 "// BaseException's attributes (exceptions.c's BaseException_getset and members)"] [694 1 "// unpackAll is the items of an iterable."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[64 32] [68 32] [107 31] [134 31] [138 28] [142 35] [1